meta {
  name: Analyze Write
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/write-requests/analyze
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "connectionId": "{{connectionId}}",
    "writeSql": "ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN note text;\nCREATE INDEX idx_orders_note ON orders(note);"
  }
}

docs {
  Classify a draft write without touching the database: whether it's a single-statement DML or a multi-statement / DDL migration, the statement count, whether it contains DDL, whether it needs the no-rollback escape hatch (a statement that can't run in a transaction, e.g. CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY / VACUUM), and any hard block. Powers the composer's live feedback (disabling the verify SELECT and showing the "Run without rollback" toggle).

  Read-only; no DB mutation. Returns { statementCount, isMigration, hasDdl, requiresNoTransaction, blocked? }.

  Requires a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}) and write access to the connection's environment.
}
